<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $414.2 mln Dec 27.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $414.2 mln Dec 27.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $414.2 million deficit on December 27 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON DECEMBER 27</p>
<p>Exports: $243.7 million</p>
<p>Imports: $233 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $561.2 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $986.1 million</p>
<p>Deficit: $414.2 million</p>
<p>DECEMBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $4.052 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $4.054 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $9.373 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $6.383 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $2.988 billion</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>(-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo Newsroom, 5511 2485415)</p>
